    "equivalent": true,
    "why": "EQUIVALENT, AND THE MOD'S `>` IS KEPT FOR SHAPE NOT BEHAVIOUR. At the boundary the two agree: newProgress == 100 gives rollUp 0, so `added` is the whole value either way and nothing carries. The Lua writes `>` (helper.lua:126) and the port restates it, but no reachable state tells them apart - the only difference is whether `levelRollUp` is written a 0, which every reader takes through `?? 0`."
  },
